<!--
  Akai Professional APC mini mk2: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    APC mini mk2 Communications Protocol (v1.0) (Akai Professional (inMusic Brands), 2023-01-23 (PDF date)), pages 2 (Pad/Button Values, pad matrix figure), 15 (Control Mapping: buttons), 16 (Channel Faders / Master Fader)
    https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/akai/attachments/APC%20mini%20mk2%20-%20Communication%20Protocol%20-%20v1.0.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.
  label="..." is the control's name on the unit, shown in the mapping dialog and the guided tour.

  BEFORE YOU START: None needed for these binds: faders and Track buttons send on USB Port 0, MIDI channel 1, in every mode.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): 8x8 clip-launch pad grid (notes 0x00-0x3F): not bound, see doubts. The note layout is clear (bottom row 0x00-0x07 left to right, up to top row 0x38-0x3F), but the inbound MIDI channel in Session View is not stated.; Scene Launch 1-8 (notes 0x70-0x77, channel 1): left free.; Shift (note 0x7A, channel 1): left free.

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
<CadenceMidiMap name="Akai Professional APC mini mk2" maker="Akai Professional" model="APC mini mk2" match="apcminimk2" version="2">
  <bind target="ch1.gain" kind="0" ch="1" num="48" label="Channel Fader 1" status="manual"/>  <!-- Channel Fader 1, p.16 -->
  <bind target="ch2.gain" kind="0" ch="1" num="49" label="Channel Fader 2" status="manual"/>  <!-- Channel Fader 2, p.16 -->
